Mark where a fillet's trim curve touches an edge of the face it trims.

What it fixes
  A fillet or chamfer whose contact curve on a support face ends exactly
  on another edge of that face - a through hole whose rim is tangent to
  the fillet's foot - builds IsDone() with the trimmed face's outer wire
  touching its inner wire at a point no vertex marks. Every curve in it
  is right and the volume is the volume a point contact gives, but
  BRepCheck_Analyzer rejects the face (IntersectingWires), the mesh of it
  is not watertight, and a boolean on it fails. ChFi3d writes its own
  interferences into the TopOpeBRepDS data structure (ChFi3d_FilDS), and
  recorded the contact curve's ends on the arcs they land on but never a
  touch along its length.

  Three changes, two of them in the builder the fillet relies on:

  - ChFi3d_Builder_0.cxx, ChFi3d_TouchesOnFace: after a stripe's contact
    curve is written on a face, the curve's pcurve is intersected with
    every edge of that face in the face's parameter space, the test
    BRepCheck_Face itself runs (Geom2dInt_GInter at 1e-10). A meeting
    inside both, where the edge stays on one side of the curve through
    the point, is a touch: one data-structure point, a leaving and an
    entering interference on the curve and on the edge at that parameter,
    and the edge's other faces added to the data structure. A crossing is
    left alone, as is a contact at a vertex.
  - TopOpeBRepBuild_PaveSet::HasEqualParameters: two paves of one vertex
    at one parameter, leaving and entering, are the edge passing through
    the vertex, not a closed edge cut there. Before, the pair rotated a
    closed edge to start at the touch and the edge's own seam vertex,
    landing inside the rotated range, lost the half of the rim after it:
    7297.122 mm^3, a shell that would not close.
  - TopOpeBRepBuild_Builder::ToSplit: a face in the data structure is
    rebuilt when one of its edges carries geometry, so an edge cut on one
    face is cut on every face it bounds. Before, the hole's cylindrical
    face kept the whole rim while the floor had its two pieces: three free
    edges, BRepCheck_NotClosed on the shell.

How it was measured
  A 40 x 30 x 5 base with a 3 x 30 x 15 fin across it, a diameter 5 through
  hole at x = 6 so the rim meets the fillet's foot at (3.5, 0, 5), and a
  2 mm fillet on the fin's two root edges; the same with the hole at
  x = 8 (clear) and x = 5.5 (0.5 mm into the foot, where the fillet
  surface meets the hole's cylinder and is trimmed by it). Stock 8.0.1:
  touch IsDone, BRepCheck invalid, 7303.330 mm^3, 22 vertices, 33 edges.
  Patched: touch valid, 7303.330 mm^3, 23 vertices, 35 edges, all four
  edges at the contact sharing one vertex; clear and overlap unchanged
  (valid, 7303.330 and 7303.151 mm^3, 33 and 40 edges). parcad's
  eval/cases/fillet-ends-on-a-hole-rim.json and its two controls hold
  the numbers; the full corpus (210 cases) builds the same before and
  after.

Upstream status
  Not yet reported. Should be offered as an issue with the three parts
  above and the box-fin-hole model.

